reason nasu lula da silva was leading  the polls in 2018.  the left-wing political leader would  have probably been elected brazil's  president  for the third time had he not been  convicted  on corruption charges and banned from  running  now lula is back in the political scene  as the country faces  its worst moment in the covet 19  pandemic  and he poses a serious threat to  right-wing president  jair bolsonaro in next year's elections  it's good news that comes at the right  time because the political situation in  the country is so dire  i would not believe a politician who has  already been arrested for corruption  and i don't think lula is the right  person to run our country  lula has always said that he was wrongly  convicted and imprisoned  he says the bribery money laundering and  corruption charges  were part of a scheme to strip him of  his political rights  after years of judicial battle a supreme  court judge on monday  annulled the convictions against lula  the decision has nothing to do with  lula's innocence or guilt  the supreme court judge argued that the  former president had been tried in the  southern city of kurichiba  when he should have been tried in the  capital brasilia  it may be a technicality but one that  could be shaped  brazil's political and judicial  landscape  the fact is that lula can now run for  the presidency  and he still has the support of half of  brazil's voters  according to a recent poll some of them  took to the streets to celebrate  and to protest against what they call  president bolsonaro's mishandling of the  pandemic  lula reacted on twitter saying the  annulment of the charges  proves he has always been right while  bolsonaro accused the supreme court  judge  of acting on behalf of the workers party  brazil's political divisions deepening  in the midst of a deadly pandemic  monika yanakiv al-jazeera rio de janeiro
 

